course: dictionary
lesson: 10688
title: Unquestioned: accepted without doubt
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Unquestioned means accepted as true or right, with no doubt. The clue is in the parts: un- means not, and questioned means asked about, so unquestioned means not asked about. «Her talent was unquestioned» means everybody agrees she is talented, and nobody argues.
explain: The word has a second meaning, about checking. Something unquestioned has not been asked about or tested. In science, ideas should not stay unquestioned. Scientists test them and change their minds when the evidence says so.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The Rat lets him rest unquestioned» means the Rat does not ask the traveller anything first. In Alice in Wonderland, the Queen of Hearts' orders go unquestioned until Alice says «Nonsense!». Swap in your meaning: "the orders are accepted without doubt" still fits the story.
fact: Un- at the start of a word means not, so unquestioned means not questioned.
fact: «Unquestioned» means accepted as true or right, with no doubt.
fact: «Unquestioned» can also mean not asked about or not checked.
fact: Other un- words work the same way: unknown, unhappy and unfair each mean "not" the rest of the word.
fact: The opposite of unquestioned is questioned, which means doubted, asked about or tested.
exercise: «Her talent was unquestioned.» What does unquestioned mean here? | *Everybody agrees it is true, with no doubt | She asked too many questions | It was hidden away | Nobody can find it
exercise: What does the un- in unquestioned mean? | *Not | Very | Again | Before
exercise: In Alice in Wonderland the Queen of Hearts' orders go unquestioned. What happens when Alice says «Nonsense!»? | *The orders are challenged and questioned | Alice falls asleep | The orders are accepted by everyone | The Queen wins a prize
test: Why should scientists not leave their ideas unquestioned? | To make the ideas longer | Because ideas cannot be tested | *To test them and change them if needed | Because questions are rude
test: Which word is the opposite of unquestioned? | ancient | quietly | proud | *questioned
exam: In «the Rat lets him rest unquestioned», what does the Rat do? | Asks the traveller to leave at once | *Lets the traveller rest without asking him questions first | Gives him a big dinner | Shouts at him for arriving
